    "promptSnippet": "# Aster Component Implementation Prompt — Link\n\n## 1. Component Purpose & Canonical Role\n- **Component:** Link (`link`)\n- **Category:** Navigation & Layout\n- **Native Element:** `<a>`\n- **Summary:** An underlined link for moving to another page or place.\n- **When to Use:** Moving to another page or place, including links within text.\n- **When Not to Use:** Actions such as saving or deleting. Use Button instead.\n\n## 2. Authoritative Repository Files\n- **Component CSS:** `components/link/link.css`\n- **Component Spec:** `docs/components/link.md`\n- **Agent Contract:** `skills/using-aster-components/SKILL.md`\n- **Compiled Bundle:** `dist/css/aster.css`\n\n## 3. Canonical HTML Structure & Classes\n```html\n<a class=\"as-link\" href=\"/docs/installation\">Read the installation guide</a>\n\n<a class=\"as-link as-link--muted\" href=\"/docs/principles\">Core principles</a>\n```\n\n## 4. Measured Geometry\nMeasured from the rendered component when this page loads.\n\n## 5. Non-Negotiable Aster Constraints\n1. Bind colors to `--as-semantic-color-*` tokens, never primitives or hex values.\n2. Use the radius tokens, with 4px as the smallest component radius.\n3. Aster has one standard density, with no compact mode.\n4. Keep text at 4.5:1 contrast and interactive elements keyboard operable.\n\n## 6. Verification Commands\n```bash\nnpm run test:components\nnpm run test:browser\n```",
